- **STATUS CODE REPORTING THE WRAPPER / check that cannot fail**: line 117.  
  Exact input: `contradicted_refusals.json` = `{"fixed":[{"page":"p.html"}]}`, `p.html` = `<html></html>`, run with `--apply`.  
  Consequence: line 72 silently skips the missing panel and the process still exits 0, so a gate can pass with zero restatements.

- **INSTRUMENT READING A DIFFERENT OBJECT**: lines 55-58.  
  Exact input:
  ```html
  <section class="panel" id="pn-search">
  <table><tr><td>query metadata</td></tr></table>
  <table><caption>Table 2. ClinicalTrials.gov API v2</caption></table>
  </section>
  ```
  Consequence: a non-yield table makes the panel look `HELD`, leaving the empty yield table unexplained.

- **IDEMPOTENCY GUARD SATISFIED BY ITS OWN COMMENT OR MARKER**: line 75.  
  Exact input:
  ```html
  <section class="panel" id="pn-search">
  <!-- absent-state TODO -->
  <table><caption>Table 2. ClinicalTrials.gov API v2</caption></table>
  </section>
  ```
  Consequence: the substring in a comment prevents insertion of the actual absent-state note.

- **SELECTOR KEYED TO A FORM THE CORPUS MAY NOT USE**: lines 55 and 59.  
  Exact input:
  ```html
  <section class="panel" id="pn-search">
  <table class="ctgov"><caption>Table 2</caption><tr><td>NCT1</td></tr></table>
  </section>
  ```
  Consequence: `<table class=...>` is ignored, so a populated table is treated as empty and gets a false `PARTIALLY_HELD` note.

- **VALUES COMPARED AS TEXT/BYTES WHERE LINE ENDINGS DIFFER**: lines 82-84.  
  Exact input:
  ```html
  <section class="panel" id="pn-search">\r\n<table><caption>Table 2</caption></table>
  </section>
  ```
  Consequence: the semantic opener exists, but the LF-only byte anchor is not found, so the panel is skipped.

